No upstream source: this DidYouMean RBS extras stub is hand-written
by Rigor maintainers under MPL-2.0 (matching the rest of Rigor).
The rbs gem ships `stdlib/did_you_mean/0/did_you_mean.rbs` already
(loaded via `did_you_mean` in `Environment::DEFAULT_LIBRARIES`),
but four top-level singleton methods (`DidYouMean.formatter`,
`DidYouMean.formatter=`, `DidYouMean.spell_checkers`,
`DidYouMean.correct_error`) are missing.

This file is a SUPPLEMENT — it re-opens the upstream module to
ADD the missing declarations only, never redeclaring anything
the upstream RBS already covers, so the loader does not raise
`RBS::DuplicatedDeclarationError`.

Modelled on `references/ruby/lib/did_you_mean.rb`'s `class << self`
block.
